{"attempts":[],"task":{"current":1,"errors":"[]","flags":"[]","id":"gh:1334213602","input_hash":"sha256:a71081f637a9af0c6a0613176a8ca67732239f5844e5a2daebdd652a40f58a44","output":null,"payload":"{\"metadata\":{\"description\":\"Guide Dog for DSH — MiniMax multimodal plugin: image/video/music/speech generation & vision tools, voice mode, voice input. Real-time call mode implemented: streaming voice conversation, unified floating UI, adaptive prompts, zh/en i18n. Accessibility features planned for testing\",\"id\":\"gh:1334213602\",\"install_available\":true,\"language\":\"JavaScript\",\"name\":\"dsh-guide-dog\",\"slug\":\"AtropinolTT/dsh-guide-dog\",\"topics\":[\"dsh\",\"dsh-plugin\",\"minimax\",\"multimodal\",\"tts\",\"voice-input\"]},\"paragraphs\":[{\"id\":\"p1s1\",\"text\":\"Guide Dog for DSH — MiniMax multimodal plugin: image/video/music/speech generation & vision tools, v\"},{\"id\":\"p1s2\",\"text\":\"oice mode, voice input. Real-time call mode implemented: streaming voice conversation, unified float\"},{\"id\":\"p1s3\",\"text\":\"ing UI, adaptive prompts, zh/en i18n. Accessibility features planned for testing\"},{\"id\":\"p2s1\",\"text\":\"# Guide Dog for DSH, powered by MiniMax\"},{\"id\":\"p3s1\",\"text\":\"**English** | 简体中文\"},{\"id\":\"p4s1\",\"text\":\"A dynamic Cordis plugin that gives DeepSeek Harness multimodal superpowers through\\nthe mmx CLI (Mini\"},{\"id\":\"p4s2\",\"text\":\"amic Cordis plugin that gives DeepSeek Harness multimodal superpowers through\\nthe mmx CLI (MiniMax):\"},{\"id\":\"p5s1\",\"text\":\"- **Eyes for DeepSeek** — MiniMax VLM (`guide_dog_vision` / `guide_dog_inspect`)\\ndescribes images, s\"},{\"id\":\"p5s2\",\"text\":\"o a model with no native vision input (e.g. DeepSeek) can\\nstill review frontend designs, figures, sc\"},{\"id\":\"p5s3\",\"text\":\"reenshots, and generated images.\\n- **Hands for generation** — images (`image-01`), video (`MiniMax-H\"},{\"id\":\"p5s4\",\"text\":\"3` / Hailuo),\\nspeech (MiniMax TTS), music (`music-3.0`), text (`MiniMax-M3`), and web search.\\n- **We\"},{\"id\":\"p5s5\",\"text\":\"b UI preview & playback** — every generated file is served same-origin at\\n`/guide-dog/media/<file>` \"},{\"id\":\"p5s6\",\"text\":\"and rendered inline in the conversation tool cards\\n(`<img>`, `<audio controls>`, `<video controls>`)\"},{\"id\":\"p5s7\",\"text\":\", plus a **Guide Dog**\\nsettings page with auth status and a speak tester.\\n- **Skill integration** — \"},{\"id\":\"p5s8\",\"text\":\"`guide_dog_speak` reuses your existing\\n`audio-conversation` and\\n`speech-mmx` skill pipelines\\n(text t\"},{\"id\":\"p5s9\",\"text\":\"ransform, CJK auto-detect, per-language voices, host playback),\\nand falls back to raw `mmx speech sy\"},{\"id\":\"p5s10\",\"text\":\"nthesize` when the skill scripts are absent.\\n- **Automatic invocation** — a mounted system-prompt se\"},{\"id\":\"p5s11\",\"text\":\"ction\\n(`guide-dog-vision`, order 110) tells the agent to auto-invoke the inspection\\ntools for any jo\"},{\"id\":\"p5s12\",\"text\":\"b needing visual checks, especially when the active model\\ncannot see images.\\n- **Call mode (Phase 2,\"},{\"id\":\"p5s13\",\"text\":\" shipped)** — hands-free, real-time voice conversation\\nin the web UI: VAD / push-to-talk turn-taking\"},{\"id\":\"p5s14\",\"text\":\", streaming sentence-level TTS\\nwith barge-in, consensus-first protection for write commands, progres\"},{\"id\":\"p5s15\",\"text\":\"s\\nannouncements, and a unified floating dual-pill UI at the composer with\\nzh/en i18n (details in \\\"Ph\"},{\"id\":\"p5s16\",\"text\":\"ase 2 — call mode\\\" below).\\n[该节后续省略]\"},{\"id\":\"p6s1\",\"text\":\"## Featured\"},{\"id\":\"p7s1\",\"text\":\"Guide Dog is featured in dsh-recommend,\\na community-curated plugin directory for DSH. It passed the \"},{\"id\":\"p7s2\",\"text\":\"project's\\ncertification review and carries the gold **certified** badge at the top of\\nthis README; t\"},{\"id\":\"p7s3\",\"text\":\"he score badge updates automatically on every registry sync.\"},{\"id\":\"p8s1\",\"text\":\"### Feature list\"},{\"id\":\"p9s1\",\"text\":\"- **Voice mode (host event-driven)** — a host `session/event` listener watches\\n`assistant/message` e\"},{\"id\":\"p9s2\",\"text\":\"vents, extracts the reply text\\n(`event.data.content` blocks with `type === 'text'`), checks whether \"},{\"id\":\"p9s3\",\"text\":\"voice\\nmode is effective for that session (session override else global default),\\nand enqueues the TT\"},{\"id\":\"p9s4\",\"text\":\"S result (`{url, key}`) or error into a per-session\\n`voiceQueue`. The client polls the queue every s\"},{\"id\":\"p9s5\",\"text\":\"econd and plays it with a\\nmodule-level `Audio` object, or shows a bottom-right toast + beep for 6s.\\n\"},{\"id\":\"p9s6\",\"text\":\"- **Voice cluster** — `conversation.input.left` entry `guide-dog-voice`\\n(order 30) at the input box'\"},{\"id\":\"p9s7\",\"text\":\"s bottom-left, themed with DSH tokens\\n(`--dsw-alias-*`), inheriting the app font:\\n- small **speaker*\"},{\"id\":\"p9s8\",\"text\":\"* icon — click toggles the per-session voice-mode override\\n(`guide-dog/set-config` with `voiceMode.s\"},{\"id\":\"p9s9\",\"text\":\"essions`); hover tooltip shows\\n\\\"Voice mode: on/off · Global default: on/off\\\".\\n- **language dropdown*\"},{\"id\":\"p9s10\",\"text\":\"* — recognition language detection (auto/zh/en).\\n- **mic** icon — record → transcribe → insert (feat\"},{\"id\":\"p9s11\",\"text\":\"her-style SVG; recording\\nstate pulses red with a second counter).\\n- **Session-scoped playback** — pl\"},{\"id\":\"p9s12\",\"text\":\"ayback runs on a module-level `Audio`\\nobject, so switching sessions never replays or interrupts it: \"},{\"id\":\"p9s13\",\"text\":\"the current\\nclip plays to the end unless a new playback task (a fresh queue entry from\\nany session) \"},{\"id\":\"p9s14\",\"text\":\"overrides it.\\n- **Mic voice input** — the mic in the cluster: MediaRecorder with 1s\\ntimeslices, live\"},{\"id\":\"p9s15\",\"text\":\" second counter, maxSeconds auto-stop, language from the\\ndropdown, and transcribe via `guide-dog/tra\"},{\"id\":\"p9s16\",\"text\":\"nscribe`. Recognized text is\\ninserted into the input box with `inputActions.setDraft(text)` (auto-se\"},{\"id\":\"p9s17\",\"text\":\"nd\\nvia `inputActions.submit()` when configured). Error states: `mic_denied`,\\n`no_device`, `empty_spe\"},{\"id\":\"p9s18\",\"text\":\"ech`, `stt_failed`, `stt_timeout`,\\n`engine_unavailable`, `insert_failed` (never silent).\\n- **Recorde\"},{\"id\":\"p9s19\",\"text\":\"r page** — sandboxed clients that cannot record in-page get a\\n`🎙 Open recorder page` link to the sta\"},{\"id\":\"p9s20\",\"text\":\"ndalone `/guide-dog/recorder` page\\n(GET serves a self-contained HTML recorder; POST\\n`/guide-dog/tran\"},{\"id\":\"p9s21\",\"text\":\"scribe-upload` accepts raw `audio/webm`, 20 MB cap, and runs\\nthe same `transcribeImpl`).\\n[该节后续省略]\"},{\"id\":\"p10s1\",\"text\":\"### Feature list\"},{\"id\":\"p11s1\",\"text\":\"- **WebSocket-free dual channel** — uplink is a whole-clip POST\\n`/guide-dog/call-transcribe` (webm/o\"},{\"id\":\"p11s2\",\"text\":\"pus, ≤20MB, reuses the Phase 1\\n`transcribeImpl` and the local whisper pipeline) → `{ok, text, langua\"},{\"id\":\"p11s3\",\"text\":\"ge,\\ndurationMs}`; downlink is `GET /guide-dog/tts-stream` over a chunked HTTP\\nstream (the host spawn\"},{\"id\":\"p11s4\",\"text\":\"s `mmx speech synthesize --stream --format pcm\\n--sample-rate 24000` per sentence and pipes stdout in\"},{\"id\":\"p11s5\",\"text\":\"crementally into\\n`res.write`; the client reads the stream with `fetch().body.getReader()`\\n→ PCM→WAV \"},{\"id\":\"p11s6\",\"text\":\"→ seamless Web Audio scheduling). No new WebSocket protocol\\nsurface on the transport layer; browser \"},{\"id\":\"p11s7\",\"text\":\"and CLI reuse the same pipeline.\\n- **Automatic VAD + push-to-talk (PTT)** — default VAD (`call.mode=\"},{\"id\":\"p11s8\",\"text\":\"'vad'`):\\nMediaRecorder (`audio/webm;codecs=opus`, 250ms timeslice, continuous\\nrecording) + a paralle\"},{\"id\":\"p11s9\",\"text\":\"l AnalyserNode energy detector (RMS ≥\\n`vad.threshold`; silence for `vad.silenceMs` ends an utterance\"},{\"id\":\"p11s10\",\"text\":\";\\n`vad.minSpeechMs` minimum speech; `vad.maxSegmentSeconds` per-segment cap)\\n— speak-pause-speak aut\"},{\"id\":\"p11s11\",\"text\":\"omatically becomes two turns; the panel can switch\\nto `ptt` push-to-talk (hold the mic to talk, rele\"},{\"id\":\"p11s12\",\"text\":\"ase to send; VAD\\nparameters do not participate in endpointing, only in interruption\\nmonitoring).\\n- *\"},{\"id\":\"p11s13\",\"text\":\"*Consensus-first (core interaction paradigm)** — active only when\\ncall/a11y is on; typing mode keeps\"},{\"id\":\"p11s14\",\"text\":\" the Phase 1 behavior: a prompt soft\\nconstraint (`guide_dog_call_consensus` systemPrompt variable, c\"},{\"id\":\"p11s15\",\"text\":\"onversational\\nwording: understand intent first, ask when unclear, explain before\\n[该节后续省略]\"},{\"id\":\"p12s1\",\"text\":\"## Security notes\"},{\"id\":\"p13s1\",\"text\":\"- Media dir inside the workspace root → no sandbox widening required.\\n- The route serves only plugin\"},{\"id\":\"p13s2\",\"text\":\"-owned media with allowlisted extensions.\\n- The MiniMax API key stays in mmx's own config (`~/.mmx/c\"},{\"id\":\"p13s3\",\"text\":\"onfig.json`); the\\nplugin never reads or forwards it.\\n- Host playback uses the raw `subprocess` servi\"},{\"id\":\"p13s4\",\"text\":\"ce (players must outlive the\\nsandbox's `--die-with-parent` bwrap profile); each new playback termina\"},{\"id\":\"p13s5\",\"text\":\"tes the\\nprevious one.\"}],\"truncated\":true}","review_level":null,"review_reason":null,"reviewed_at":null,"source":"{\"headSha\":\"fbd3a0584609722052710978214f8edceeb458a2\",\"metadataHash\":\"sha256:d07b54fd0a2bd8af2e6f98f1120927df47a90b64d0abf20fc1a7e95fc931e5e0\",\"path\":\"README.md\",\"rawHash\":\"026cc4ccac32771d318142a294e89bddd6fcdeafe8572eb1c6295e58afa4159d\",\"registryRevision\":\"sha256:04371b59939b1f07e53deb93a538f88188886638c931cd7ba7b544bd1ef81810\"}","stars":5,"status":"prepared","updated":"2026-11-13T07:16:20.815434+00:00","versions":"{\"cleaner\":\"3\",\"model\":\"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash\",\"prompt\":\"5\",\"reasoning\":\"low\",\"schema\":\"5\",\"taxonomy\":\"1\"}"}}
